/T (Functional overview: - TCNT resets to 0 when PRESETn = 0. - If count_enable = 1, counting begins. - When count_load = 1, the counter loads count_start_value from TDR. - Output TCNT[7:0] reflects the current counter value. - Overflow and underflow events are detected and trigger TMR_OVF or TMR_UDF flags. - These flags are stored in the Timer Status Register \(TSR\) for software access.)
/E (Functional overview: - TCNT resets to 0 when PRESETn = 0. - If count_enable = 1, counting begins. - When count_load = 1, the counter loads count_start_value from TDR. - Output TCNT[7:0] reflects the current counter value. - Overflow and underflow events are detected and trigger TMR_OVF or TMR_UDF flags. - These flags are stored in the Timer Status Register \(TSR\) for software access.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
